<ul dir="auto">
<li><strong>A simpler dashboard.</strong> At the top: the MRR with its change over 30 days, your goal (or the paying customers of one project), where the MRR went, then what to act on: the money to recover from failed payments, and where the trials lead (paid, card refused, cancelled).</li>
<li>Revenue per customer, lifetime value and the churn percentages leave the top of the page: on small numbers they said little. Churn keeps its chart further down.</li>
</ul>
